hadiths[14]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16672","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn al-Harith, from Khallad ibn al-Saib ibn Khallad, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and said: Order your companions to raise their voices with ihlal. Sufyan once said: Jibril (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and commanded me to order my companions to raise their voices with ihlal."
"16673","Anas ibn Iyad al-Laythi Abu Damrah said, he said: Yazid ibn Khusayfah narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sasah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from al-Saib ibn Khallad that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever frightens the people of Madinah wrongfully, Allah will frighten him, and upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Allah will not accept from him on the Day of Resurrection sarf nor adl."
"16674","He said: Waki narrated to us, he said: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, from Khallad ibn al-Saib, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever plants a crop and birds or wayfarers eat from it, it shall be charity for him thereby."
"16675","He said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Muslim ibn Abi Maryam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from al-Saib ibn Khallad that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever frightens the people of Madinah, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will frighten him, and upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Allah will not accept from him on the Day of Resurrection sarf nor adl."
"16676","He said: Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Had, narrated to me, from Abu Bakr ibn al-Munkadir, from Ata ibn Yasar, from al-Saib ibn Khallad, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Nothing befalls the believer, even the thorn that pricks him, except Allah writes for him thereby a good deed and removes thereby a sin from him."
"16677","He said: Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Bakr ibn Sawadah al-Judhami, from Salih ibn Khaywan, from Abu Sahlah al-Saib ibn Khallad that a man led people and spat in the qiblah while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was looking. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when he finished: He shall not lead you in prayer. He later wished to lead them, but they prevented him and informed him of the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Yes. And I thought he said: You have harmed Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"16678","He said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Abi Maryam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from al-Saib ibn Khallad, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever frightens Madinah, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will frighten him, and upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Allah will not accept from him sarf nor adl."
"16679","He said: Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Habban ibn Wasi, from Khallad ibn al-Saib al-Ansari that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he supplicated, would place the insides of his palms toward his face."
"16680","He said: Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Habban ibn Wasi, from Khallad ibn al-Saib al-Ansari that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he asked, would place the insides of his palms toward him, and when he sought refuge, would place their backs toward him."
"16681","He said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Jafar informed us, he said: Yazid informed me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sasah al-Ansari that Ata ibn Yasar informed him that al-Saib ibn Khallad, brother of Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever frightens the people of Madinah as a wrongdoer, Allah will frighten him, and upon him shall be the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Neither adl nor sarf shall be accepted from him."
"16682","He said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Labid, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, from al-Saib ibn Khallad that Jibril, peace be upon him, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Be clamorous with talbiyah and profuse with sacrifice. Al-ajj is talbiyah, and al-thajj is slaughtering camels."
"16683","He said: I recited to Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi: Malik narrated to us, and Rawh narrated to us, he said: Malik, meaning Ibn Anas, narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Khallad ibn al-Saib al-Ansari, from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and said that I order my companions, or those with me, to raise their voices with talbiyah or ihlal, meaning one of the two."
"16684","He said: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, and Rawh, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm wrote to me saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn al-Harith narrated to me that Khallad ibn al-Saib ibn Suwayd al-Ansari narrated to him, from his father al-Saib ibn Khallad that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and said: Allah commands you to order your companions to raise their voices with talbiyah and ihlal. Rawh said: With talbiyah or ihlal. He said: I do not know which of us erred, I and Abdullah, or Khallad, in ihlal or talbiyah."
"16685","Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn al-Harith, from Khallad ibn al-Saib ibn Khallad, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and said: Order your companions to raise their voices with ihlal."
